WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.461
- Good morning believe nation!

00:00:04.461 --> 00:00:05.770
Today we're going to talk about

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.188
how to deal with jealousy.

00:00:08.188 --> 00:00:10.103
As always guys as you're
watching the clips

00:00:10.103 --> 00:00:11.769
if you hear somebody say something

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:13.358
that really resonates with you,

00:00:13.358 --> 00:00:15.120
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.133
and put quotes around it

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.048
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:18.048 --> 00:00:19.515
Also when you write it down

00:00:19.515 --> 00:00:22.731
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself too.

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:23.564
Enjoy.

00:00:23.564 --> 00:00:27.231
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:43.135 --> 00:00:45.210
- [Narrator] It's that
knot in your stomach

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.413
that mix of fear and anxiety

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.285
that materializes when you feel threatened

00:00:49.285 --> 00:00:51.606
by someone prettier than
you, smarter than you,

00:00:51.606 --> 00:00:52.746
it can cause you to do

00:00:52.746 --> 00:00:55.275
some pretty stupid, sit-com level stuff

00:00:55.275 --> 00:00:56.739
just to regain control,

00:00:56.739 --> 00:00:59.221
things that usually hurt other people too.

00:00:59.221 --> 00:01:01.664
You're probably familiar with this feeling

00:01:01.664 --> 00:01:04.475
it's what Shakespeare called
the green-eyed monster

00:01:04.475 --> 00:01:07.160
today, we're talking about jealousy.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.784
Here's the thing kids,

00:01:08.784 --> 00:01:12.087
jealousy is a distinctly
first person emotion.

00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:15.915
It almost always comes
from a place of insecurity

00:01:15.915 --> 00:01:18.161
which you ultimately project on others.

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:21.868
The bottom line, jealousy
isn't about the other person

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:22.803
it's about you.

00:01:22.803 --> 00:01:24.064
Jealousy tends to come with

00:01:24.064 --> 00:01:26.346
a specific set of blinders

00:01:26.346 --> 00:01:28.137
and the more jealous we are

00:01:28.137 --> 00:01:30.865
the less able we are to, let's say,

00:01:30.865 --> 00:01:33.230
empathize with others.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:36.156
For example, a study
conducted by the researchers

00:01:36.156 --> 00:01:39.622
at the University of Delaware
found that jealous people

00:01:39.622 --> 00:01:41.983
were more easily distracted

00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:45.077
and less able to perform
simple memory games.

00:01:45.077 --> 00:01:46.912
So let's try to figure out

00:01:46.912 --> 00:01:50.745
how to get your jealousy
issues under control.

00:01:54.849 --> 00:01:56.401
- You know if you're coming from a place

00:01:56.401 --> 00:01:57.583
that fear of inadequacy,

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.252
thinking someone's going to leave you,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.051
it often comes from a place

00:02:01.051 --> 00:02:04.134
of you're not giving yourself credit.

00:02:04.997 --> 00:02:06.625
You know you do good things,

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:09.148
but you don't feel and integrate
those into your identity

00:02:09.148 --> 00:02:12.077
so that you become a stronger,
happier, healthier adult.

00:02:12.077 --> 00:02:13.381
A lot of people,

00:02:13.381 --> 00:02:15.327
they're actually pretty
extraordinary people,

00:02:15.327 --> 00:02:17.045
but they don't feel extraordinary,

00:02:17.045 --> 00:02:19.779
because all those extraordinary
things that happen

00:02:19.779 --> 00:02:21.485
they never integrate it.

00:02:21.485 --> 00:02:22.583
Someone gives them a compliment,

00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:24.088
they're like yeah yeah yeah whatever,

00:02:24.088 --> 00:02:25.023
and they can't hear it,

00:02:25.023 --> 00:02:27.221
it doesn't penetrate into their identity

00:02:27.221 --> 00:02:30.927
where they start going,
you know what, I'm alright,

00:02:30.927 --> 00:02:32.966
I am good, I can be confident now,

00:02:32.966 --> 00:02:34.631
I've achieved enough,
I've come far enough,

00:02:34.631 --> 00:02:36.277
I've survived enough.

00:02:36.277 --> 00:02:38.721
It's about giving yourself credit

00:02:38.721 --> 00:02:40.022
and remembering your strengths.

00:02:40.022 --> 00:02:42.065
You've come through such difficult things

00:02:42.065 --> 00:02:45.204
in your life that you're
stronger than you know.

00:02:45.204 --> 00:02:46.708
So why is that so important?

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:49.076
Because you know what,
if they do leave ya,

00:02:49.076 --> 00:02:51.475
you'll be fine, and that
is the hardest thing

00:02:51.475 --> 00:02:53.684
to believe when you have
this fear of jealousy.

00:02:53.684 --> 00:02:57.196
They're going to leave,
and I might be wrecked.

00:02:57.196 --> 00:02:59.966
You won't be wrecked, you've
survived a lot in the past,

00:02:59.966 --> 00:03:01.921
someone's probably already
left you in your life

00:03:01.921 --> 00:03:05.016
not to be a blamer or making fun of you

00:03:05.016 --> 00:03:06.447
it's just true right?

00:03:06.447 --> 00:03:07.997
Lots of people have walked out on me,

00:03:07.997 --> 00:03:09.096
lots of people have left me,

00:03:09.096 --> 00:03:10.563
I've had lots of breakups in my life,

00:03:10.563 --> 00:03:12.434
that happens, and I'm still here.

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:13.534
I'm still surviving.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:16.583
I'm still a pretty
annoyingly happy dude, right?

00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:20.207
You can be happy with or
without anybody or anything.

00:03:20.207 --> 00:03:22.650
You don't need more wealth,
you don't need more people,

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.847
you don't a higher career,
you don't need anything.

00:03:24.847 --> 00:03:29.337
You can choose in this moment
to feel grateful and blessed.

00:03:29.337 --> 00:03:31.088
You can choose to focus your attention

00:03:31.088 --> 00:03:32.841
on things that you appreciate,

00:03:32.841 --> 00:03:34.669
to take in the good again,

00:03:34.669 --> 00:03:37.157
and if you start taking
in those good things

00:03:37.157 --> 00:03:38.588
that you hear about yourself

00:03:38.588 --> 00:03:40.503
if you start taking in those good wins

00:03:40.503 --> 00:03:42.575
those small daily actions that you did,

00:03:42.575 --> 00:03:45.303
when you hit that goal, when
you got that project done,

00:03:45.303 --> 00:03:46.700
when you did what you were supposed to do,

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.002
when you said something nice,

00:03:48.002 --> 00:03:50.527
and start feeling stronger about yourself

00:03:50.527 --> 00:03:53.132
you stop worrying about other people

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.924
and you can start to say, you know what,

00:03:54.924 --> 00:03:57.709
with or without somebody, I'm fine.

00:03:57.709 --> 00:03:59.621
'Cause you know what that makes you?

00:03:59.621 --> 00:04:00.645
Attractive.

00:04:00.645 --> 00:04:02.817
- Turn envy into action.

00:04:02.817 --> 00:04:05.715
So envy can be inspiring and instructive.

00:04:05.715 --> 00:04:07.745
If you're envious of someone's results

00:04:07.745 --> 00:04:09.612
just let that fuel you ahead.

00:04:09.612 --> 00:04:12.339
The fact that they did it
means that it can be done

00:04:12.339 --> 00:04:13.595
and that you can do it too.

00:04:13.595 --> 00:04:15.749
So just give them a
high-five and a soul shake.

00:04:15.749 --> 00:04:18.721
Second, realize that envy is often a clue

00:04:18.721 --> 00:04:20.309
that there's something latent in you

00:04:20.309 --> 00:04:21.739
that needs to be expressed.

00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:24.510
So let that envy trigger
you in a beautiful way

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.098
let it guide you to where you need

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.011
to take some more action in your own life.

00:04:28.011 --> 00:04:30.333
So next time that you're feeling some envy

00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:34.500
don't feel embarrassed, just
remember this tweetable:

00:04:36.239 --> 00:04:38.519
"Don't hide your envy, ride your envy

00:04:38.519 --> 00:04:40.449
"from 'she has what I want' to

00:04:40.449 --> 00:04:42.116
"'I'll have what she's having'."

00:04:42.116 --> 00:04:46.283
- So what's the ultimate solution
to dealing with jealousy?

00:04:47.803 --> 00:04:50.522
The solution is to turn within.

00:04:50.522 --> 00:04:53.449
This is not a problem that
gets solved externally,

00:04:53.449 --> 00:04:55.450
you're not going to win the jealousy game

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:56.305
by going out there

00:04:56.305 --> 00:04:58.457
and actually defeating
that person or that thing

00:04:58.457 --> 00:05:00.164
or getting one up on them.

00:05:00.164 --> 00:05:02.153
What you need to do is you
need to actually state,

00:05:02.153 --> 00:05:03.984
Wait a minute, wait a
minute, wait a minute,

00:05:03.984 --> 00:05:07.287
this is an internal ego
struggle that I'm dealing with

00:05:07.287 --> 00:05:10.502
and I just got to turn
inwards and look inside me

00:05:10.502 --> 00:05:13.109
to see what's really going
on with my self-image,

00:05:13.109 --> 00:05:15.633
my self-esteem, my views on reality,

00:05:15.633 --> 00:05:18.039
my beliefs about myself and other people.

00:05:18.039 --> 00:05:20.706
That's where the results happen,

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.520
so don't get tricked by your ego

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:26.134
into thinking that this
is an external problem,

00:05:26.134 --> 00:05:29.434
it's not an external problem at all.

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:30.917
You have to also convince yourself

00:05:30.917 --> 00:05:34.133
that jealousy is an ego game.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.553
And that that's pretty
much what's going on here.

00:05:37.553 --> 00:05:39.961
It's not about the fact that
you're actually threatened

00:05:39.961 --> 00:05:43.542
in some serious way, it's an ego game,

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:45.215
and this is important to convince yourself

00:05:45.215 --> 00:05:47.498
because until you
convince yourself of this

00:05:47.498 --> 00:05:51.246
then you're not going
to have the awareness,

00:05:51.246 --> 00:05:54.581
consciousness, and self
honesty to look inside,

00:05:54.581 --> 00:05:57.185
and do the work that's
necessary on the inside

00:05:57.185 --> 00:05:59.055
to eradicate this jealousy.

00:05:59.055 --> 00:06:00.851
If you are able to convince yourself

00:06:00.851 --> 00:06:03.661
that this is an ego game,

00:06:03.661 --> 00:06:05.703
then you're going to
start to think like this:

00:06:05.703 --> 00:06:09.575
Oh, so it's me, there's
like elements within me

00:06:09.575 --> 00:06:11.007
that are causing this.

00:06:11.007 --> 00:06:12.802
Let me start to take a look at my ego,

00:06:12.802 --> 00:06:14.431
let me start to take a look inside

00:06:14.431 --> 00:06:17.878
and get really honest, get very observant,

00:06:17.878 --> 00:06:22.692
because there's some really
fishy, surreptitious activity

00:06:22.692 --> 00:06:26.360
going on inside my psyche, I
got to examine that for myself,

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:27.546
get a deeper look at it.

00:06:27.546 --> 00:06:30.071
Let's take a look at what's going on.

00:06:30.071 --> 00:06:32.720
Let's take a look under the hood.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:33.981
And that's the key

00:06:33.981 --> 00:06:36.268
and once you can convince yourself

00:06:36.268 --> 00:06:39.079
that looking under the
hood is a good thing

00:06:39.079 --> 00:06:40.540
and once you start to see that

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.331
Oh looking under the hood

00:06:42.331 --> 00:06:46.206
is actually not as easy
as I thought it was.

00:06:46.206 --> 00:06:48.038
That's going to take some real work.

00:06:48.038 --> 00:06:50.871
Then you've got the foundation set

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:54.509
for doing some deep inner
work on your jealousy.

00:06:54.509 --> 00:06:56.630
- If you put your mind into an environment

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:59.070
where you're constantly
thinking negative thoughts

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.754
because it's your default pattern

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:04.278
then that's what it's going to respond to.

00:07:04.278 --> 00:07:05.779
You start building the negative muscles

00:07:05.779 --> 00:07:07.083
and they'll get stronger over time,

00:07:07.083 --> 00:07:08.996
and you'll be able to lift more, heavier,

00:07:08.996 --> 00:07:11.324
negative things with those muscles.

00:07:11.324 --> 00:07:14.137
But it also works if you
put it in the positive gym,

00:07:14.137 --> 00:07:15.562
and that's what most people,

00:07:15.562 --> 00:07:18.652
all you need to do to free
yourself from negative thoughts

00:07:18.652 --> 00:07:20.781
is to get in a better environment,

00:07:20.781 --> 00:07:23.098
get your ass in the positive gym.

00:07:23.098 --> 00:07:24.242
How do you do that?

00:07:24.242 --> 00:07:25.664
Well in today's world it's easier

00:07:25.664 --> 00:07:27.257
and you don't even need to pay

00:07:27.257 --> 00:07:29.898
a fitness membership to be able to do it.

00:07:29.898 --> 00:07:32.866
So expose yourself consistently

00:07:32.866 --> 00:07:35.508
get that compass needle
and re-magnetize it

00:07:35.508 --> 00:07:37.871
in a different direction.

00:07:37.871 --> 00:07:40.432
You do it over time, you
don't walk into a gym

00:07:40.432 --> 00:07:42.921
with an overweight body
and you walk out fit.

00:07:42.921 --> 00:07:45.320
No, you walk out sore
and it's uncomfortable,

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.925
but over time that's what happens.

00:07:47.925 --> 00:07:51.548
If you want to stay with an
overweight body that's your deal

00:07:51.548 --> 00:07:52.690
and I'm here to tell you

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:54.648
if you don't make time for health

00:07:54.648 --> 00:07:56.398
you will have to make time for illness.

00:07:56.398 --> 00:07:57.786
That's not a rule I made up

00:07:57.786 --> 00:07:59.462
that's just the way it is.

00:07:59.462 --> 00:08:02.632
If you don't make time for
positivity in your life

00:08:02.632 --> 00:08:05.076
your default magnetic
north is going to swing

00:08:05.076 --> 00:08:06.624
over to the negative.

00:08:06.624 --> 00:08:09.064
I didn't make that up,
that's just the way it is,

00:08:09.064 --> 00:08:11.510
and unfortunately most
people's default north

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:12.530
points negative.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:15.865
So your environment, your
peer group, the media,

00:08:15.865 --> 00:08:18.550
all of the things that most
people are associated to

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:21.404
are constantly programming
them into a negative direction,

00:08:21.404 --> 00:08:23.808
so that when they're sleeping awake

00:08:23.808 --> 00:08:25.604
and doing things out of habit,

00:08:25.604 --> 00:08:27.144
that's the gravitational there.

00:08:27.144 --> 00:08:30.686
And then guess what, we feel
trapped by negative thinking.

00:08:30.686 --> 00:08:32.925
So how do you free yourself?

00:08:32.925 --> 00:08:35.447
Make a conscious decision.

00:08:35.447 --> 00:08:38.051
The will is what drives the thoughts

00:08:38.051 --> 00:08:41.347
so have a make a decision,
a firm resolute decision

00:08:41.347 --> 00:08:45.059
that I'm going to get my
mental ass in the positive gym.

00:08:45.059 --> 00:08:49.082
Very easy to do, surround
yourself with positive people.

00:08:49.082 --> 00:08:51.848
If you can't do that, read positive books,

00:08:51.848 --> 00:08:54.743
watch positive films,
films that lift you up

00:08:54.743 --> 00:08:57.059
that come from a place of possibility

00:08:57.059 --> 00:09:00.688
that support how we can not why I can't.

00:09:00.688 --> 00:09:03.254
If people are in your
environment that are negative

00:09:03.254 --> 00:09:04.721
start tuning them out.

00:09:04.721 --> 00:09:06.389
That's not to say that
you're better or worse

00:09:06.389 --> 00:09:08.387
it's just to say that you
want a different environment.

00:09:08.387 --> 00:09:09.612
- [Narrator] The next
time you're in a situation

00:09:09.612 --> 00:09:12.755
where you're experiencing
those extreme jealous thoughts,

00:09:12.755 --> 00:09:16.006
go into a separate room, take
out your WellCast journal

00:09:16.006 --> 00:09:17.714
and calm down.

00:09:17.714 --> 00:09:19.711
Step one, acknowledge.

00:09:19.711 --> 00:09:21.994
Admit it, you're jealous

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:24.074
and you can't run from your feelings,

00:09:24.074 --> 00:09:26.398
but by addressing your jealousy head-on

00:09:26.398 --> 00:09:28.026
you can keep it from taking on

00:09:28.026 --> 00:09:30.755
epic, unrealistic proportions.

00:09:30.755 --> 00:09:34.094
Write down exactly what's
making you jealous and why.

00:09:34.094 --> 00:09:35.686
Let's say you just found out

00:09:35.686 --> 00:09:37.106
that your two best friends

00:09:37.106 --> 00:09:38.528
didn't invite you to that movie

00:09:38.528 --> 00:09:40.446
that they caught last week,

00:09:40.446 --> 00:09:41.869
let it out.

00:09:41.869 --> 00:09:44.029
"My friends are hanging out without me,

00:09:44.029 --> 00:09:46.349
"I'm scared they'll stop being my friend."

00:09:46.349 --> 00:09:48.263
It's okay to be a little dramatic,

00:09:48.263 --> 00:09:49.770
it's just your journal.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.093
Step two, communicate.

00:09:52.093 --> 00:09:54.085
Now that all of your embarrassing thoughts

00:09:54.085 --> 00:09:57.345
are out on paper, go get the real story.

00:09:57.345 --> 00:09:59.058
Don't have an imaginary argument

00:09:59.058 --> 00:10:00.282
with your friends in your head

00:10:00.282 --> 00:10:02.356
it's only going to make things worse.

00:10:02.356 --> 00:10:04.145
Tell them how you feel
about what happened.

00:10:04.145 --> 00:10:04.978
Be vulnerable,

00:10:04.978 --> 00:10:08.130
and apologize to them if
you overreacted in any way

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:09.761
cause you might've.

00:10:09.761 --> 00:10:11.963
Make it clear that you're
expressing your feelings

00:10:11.963 --> 00:10:13.596
and not stating facts.

00:10:13.596 --> 00:10:15.712
Speak in "I" statements.

00:10:15.712 --> 00:10:18.075
"I feel like you didn't
want to hang out with me

00:10:18.075 --> 00:10:19.621
"because you're tired of me."

00:10:19.621 --> 00:10:21.013
That's your insecurity.

00:10:21.013 --> 00:10:21.909
At a certain point,

00:10:21.909 --> 00:10:23.823
the only way to get over your jealousy

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:25.781
is to stop thinking about
yourself all the time

00:10:25.781 --> 00:10:28.668
and see someone else's point of view.

00:10:28.668 --> 00:10:30.785
Step three, resolve.

00:10:30.785 --> 00:10:33.062
And this will be the hardest part for you

00:10:33.062 --> 00:10:35.576
because now you have to listen.

00:10:35.576 --> 00:10:38.261
Your friends might tell you
that you're overreacting

00:10:38.261 --> 00:10:40.624
and they might be right.

00:10:40.624 --> 00:10:42.087
"We know you don't like horror movies,

00:10:42.087 --> 00:10:44.162
"so we didn't think to invite you."

00:10:44.162 --> 00:10:45.589
- My solution to jealousy is

00:10:45.589 --> 00:10:47.485
to care less about what
other people think.

00:10:47.485 --> 00:10:48.748
I think if we're looking at jealousy

00:10:48.748 --> 00:10:51.279
there's two sides to it,

00:10:51.279 --> 00:10:52.339
there's two sides to it.

00:10:52.339 --> 00:10:55.591
The first side is people
who are jealous of you

00:10:55.591 --> 00:10:58.689
and then the second side is
people who you are jealous of.

00:10:58.689 --> 00:11:00.478
And so for people who are jealous of you,

00:11:00.478 --> 00:11:01.984
you'll find that they're often

00:11:01.984 --> 00:11:04.067
hating on you, they're telling
you you can't do things

00:11:04.067 --> 00:11:05.411
or criticizing your work

00:11:05.411 --> 00:11:07.811
where meanwhile they're not
doing anything themselves.

00:11:07.811 --> 00:11:09.358
Like the critics in your life

00:11:09.358 --> 00:11:11.839
typically have never done
what you're trying to do,

00:11:11.839 --> 00:11:14.280
and so their advice is meaningless to you,

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.809
and I recognize that if
somebody's jealous of me

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:18.644
that's their own shortcomings.

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:20.682
I don't need to let that impact

00:11:20.682 --> 00:11:22.359
what I'm going through.

00:11:22.359 --> 00:11:26.634
You get to choose how you
deal with somebody's jealousy

00:11:26.634 --> 00:11:28.184
or reactions to you,

00:11:28.184 --> 00:11:31.441
and my choice is to not
care, to let it bounce.

00:11:31.441 --> 00:11:34.122
If I fight with them on
something, what's the point?

00:11:34.122 --> 00:11:35.755
Like what do I get from that

00:11:35.755 --> 00:11:38.199
besides more negativity and more hatred

00:11:38.199 --> 00:11:40.398
and more just kind of downward spiral.

00:11:40.398 --> 00:11:41.907
And so I don't really care what

00:11:41.907 --> 00:11:43.250
people think of me.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:46.058
So that's their issue, and
they need to deal with it.

00:11:46.058 --> 00:11:47.809
Don't bring me down into your crap,

00:11:47.809 --> 00:11:49.600
I'm not getting down
into the mud with you.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.308
And the way that I don't care

00:11:51.308 --> 00:11:52.944
about these people and their opinions

00:11:52.944 --> 00:11:54.326
again is thinking about

00:11:54.326 --> 00:11:56.564
"Have they done what I am trying to do?"

00:11:56.564 --> 00:11:58.153
"Are they in any kind of position

00:11:58.153 --> 00:11:59.902
"to give me advice on this?"

00:11:59.902 --> 00:12:01.693
And usually it's nowhere even close.

00:12:01.693 --> 00:12:03.931
The people who are hating on your idea

00:12:03.931 --> 00:12:07.185
have lower standards in life than you do,

00:12:07.185 --> 00:12:08.972
so why are you listening to them?

00:12:08.972 --> 00:12:10.680
The second kind of people would be

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.943
people that you might be jealous of,

00:12:11.943 --> 00:12:13.127
people who have accomplished something

00:12:13.127 --> 00:12:14.349
that you want to accomplish

00:12:14.349 --> 00:12:16.344
or have a skill that you
want to be able to learn.

00:12:16.344 --> 00:12:19.970
And for me, I'm not jealous of anybody.

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.822
I admire people, I look up to people,

00:12:22.822 --> 00:12:24.248
I think it's because it's not just about

00:12:24.248 --> 00:12:25.548
achieving the goal,

00:12:25.548 --> 00:12:28.467
it's not just about achieving
the million subscribers,

00:12:28.467 --> 00:12:30.349
or 10 million subscribers
or whatever it is,

00:12:30.349 --> 00:12:32.874
it's not just about
achieving that revenue target

00:12:32.874 --> 00:12:35.230
that you guys have or
whatever your big goal is,

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:36.819
somebody's gone out and done it

00:12:36.819 --> 00:12:38.661
and you haven't so you're jealous of them,

00:12:38.661 --> 00:12:40.778
or somebody has that car and you don't

00:12:40.778 --> 00:12:41.915
so you're jealous of them.

00:12:41.915 --> 00:12:45.343
It's not about achieving that goal,

00:12:45.343 --> 00:12:47.139
for me, I think what helps,

00:12:47.139 --> 00:12:50.229
for me it's about the climb,
it's about the process.

00:12:50.229 --> 00:12:54.178
I look up to a Les Brown in
the public speaking field,

00:12:54.178 --> 00:12:56.299
I think he's one of the best of the best

00:12:56.299 --> 00:12:57.885
especially young Les Brown,

00:12:57.885 --> 00:13:00.369
and I admire that and I
want to learn to get better.

00:13:00.369 --> 00:13:01.714
I don't want to be Les Brown,

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:03.430
I need to be the best version of me,

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:04.775
but I like the climb,

00:13:04.775 --> 00:13:06.038
I like working on

00:13:06.038 --> 00:13:08.029
how do I get better,
and better, and better,

00:13:08.029 --> 00:13:10.962
and not just being jealous
about reaching the objective

00:13:10.962 --> 00:13:12.752
cause I want to do the
work, like I like the work.

00:13:12.752 --> 00:13:15.950
And so there's nothing that anybody has

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:18.369
that I am jealous of.

00:13:18.369 --> 00:13:21.261
And so jealousy doesn't
really play into my life.

00:13:21.261 --> 00:13:23.544
I think it really, again, comes back to

00:13:23.544 --> 00:13:26.111
enjoying the process of getting better,

00:13:26.111 --> 00:13:27.228
enjoying the growth.

00:13:27.228 --> 00:13:28.744
And if you can focus on that,

00:13:28.744 --> 00:13:30.044
and not so much the outcome

00:13:30.044 --> 00:13:31.431
then you're not going
to really be jealous.

00:13:31.431 --> 00:13:32.895
So I think depending on

00:13:32.895 --> 00:13:34.198
what kind of jealousy you're dealing with,

00:13:34.198 --> 00:13:35.868
other people being jealous of you

00:13:35.868 --> 00:13:37.451
or you being jealous of other people

00:13:37.451 --> 00:13:39.235
hopefully you've got some solutions today

00:13:39.235 --> 00:13:41.758
that can help you be less jealous

00:13:41.758 --> 00:13:45.258
and focus on the important things in life.

00:13:46.594 --> 00:13:48.582
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:48.582 --> 00:13:51.572
I made this video
because PDogB asked me to

00:13:51.572 --> 00:13:53.040
so if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.667
in the next edition of Believe Life

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:56.253
leave it down in the comments below

00:13:56.253 --> 00:13:57.477
and I'll see what I can do.

00:13:57.477 --> 00:13:59.394
I'd also love to know what did
you think about this video?

00:13:59.394 --> 00:14:00.986
What lesson did you
learn from these videos

00:14:00.986 --> 00:14:03.668
that you can apply to your
life or to your business

00:14:03.668 --> 00:14:05.048
I'd love to hear from you.

00:14:05.048 --> 00:14:06.430
And is there a strategy you have

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:07.609
on how to deal with jealousy

00:14:07.609 --> 00:14:08.954
that maybe we didn't cover

00:14:08.954 --> 00:14:10.501
leave it down in the comments below.

00:14:10.501 --> 00:14:11.679
Help out Believe Nation,

00:14:11.679 --> 00:14:12.898
do a public good,

00:14:12.898 --> 00:14:14.038
I'd love to hear from you.

00:14:14.038 --> 00:14:15.296
Finally, I wanted to
give a quick shout out

00:14:15.296 --> 00:14:17.570
to Minnie C Riley,
Minnie thank you so much

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:20.013
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word,

00:14:20.013 --> 00:14:22.256
as well as Amy's Vlog Like a Boss,

00:14:22.256 --> 00:14:24.862
I love it, make sure to read mine first,

00:14:24.862 --> 00:14:27.754
I love Amy, but you
got to read mine first,

00:14:27.754 --> 00:14:28.975
thank you for the love,

00:14:28.975 --> 00:14:29.994
thank you for the support.

00:14:29.994 --> 00:14:31.341
So thank you guys so much for watching,

00:14:31.341 --> 00:14:32.281
I believe in you,

00:14:32.281 --> 00:14:34.152
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:14:34.152 --> 00:14:35.898
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:35.898 --> 00:14:38.178
Much love, have an amazing day,

00:14:38.178 --> 00:14:40.011
and I'll see you soon.

00:14:45.829 --> 00:14:50.430
- Always remember to serve
others on your way up.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:53.721
You know, be humble and
grateful for what you have,

00:14:53.721 --> 00:14:56.938
but don't forget to also
be social with that.

00:14:56.938 --> 00:14:59.542
A lot of jealousy or the
negativity that comes at us

00:14:59.542 --> 00:15:01.008
is because people think that

00:15:01.008 --> 00:15:02.841
we're narcissistic, we're
in it for ourselves,

00:15:02.841 --> 00:15:04.672
that we don't care about anybody else,

00:15:04.672 --> 00:15:07.233
or they're jealous and
they're real insecure

00:15:07.233 --> 00:15:09.559
that we'll leave them, that
they'll get left behind,

00:15:09.559 --> 00:15:11.876
so they say these weird comments,

00:15:11.876 --> 00:15:14.641
but what they're really
saying is please don't leave.

00:15:14.641 --> 00:15:16.154
What they're really saying is,

00:15:16.154 --> 00:15:18.396
don't become somebody who's
all about the success,

00:15:18.396 --> 00:15:21.083
or the money or the fame or
the wealth or the accolades

00:15:21.083 --> 00:15:23.246
or the statues or whatever it is right.

00:15:23.246 --> 00:15:25.327
They want to know that you're still human,

00:15:25.327 --> 00:15:27.077
and the best way to demonstrate that

00:15:27.077 --> 00:15:28.830
and the most needed
thing you need to do is

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:32.980
you continue to succeed is
reach out and help those others

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:34.772
who are on the same path of life

00:15:34.772 --> 00:15:36.521
maybe just a few yards behind ya,

00:15:36.521 --> 00:15:37.947
help lift 'em up.

00:15:37.947 --> 00:15:39.616
As Booker T. Washington taught us

00:15:39.616 --> 00:15:41.531
there's two ways to exert strength,

00:15:41.531 --> 00:15:44.869
one is pushing down and
the other is pulling up.

00:15:44.869 --> 00:15:49.059
So pull some people up, help
people, offer a guiding hand,

00:15:49.059 --> 00:15:51.701
give, donate, serve, volunteer,

00:15:51.701 --> 00:15:54.472
still be out among people
serving and helping.

00:15:54.472 --> 00:15:55.944
Don't become one of those people

00:15:55.944 --> 00:15:58.266
who becomes lost in the Hollywood Hills

00:15:58.266 --> 00:16:00.348
all by yourself just
thinking about your own self

00:16:00.348 --> 00:16:01.933
staring at your belly button all day

00:16:01.933 --> 00:16:03.641
thinking how self important you are.

00:16:03.641 --> 00:16:05.639
Be that person who's still out there

00:16:05.639 --> 00:16:08.165
helping, guiding, serving, supporting,

00:16:08.165 --> 00:16:10.406
championing other people,
because you know what,

00:16:10.406 --> 00:16:12.607
you could always hate people,

00:16:12.607 --> 00:16:16.189
but it's hard to hate somebody
who's a champion of others.

00:16:16.189 --> 00:16:18.553
So you be the champion of others

00:16:18.553 --> 00:16:20.623
and soon those negative voices,

00:16:20.623 --> 00:16:21.926
those jealous people,

00:16:21.926 --> 00:16:23.721
they'll deal with their own stuff,

00:16:23.721 --> 00:16:25.226
and if they don't, ignore 'em.

00:16:25.226 --> 00:16:27.142
If they don't, keep getting better.

00:16:27.142 --> 00:16:29.022
If they don't, remember your dream.

00:16:29.022 --> 00:16:31.258
If they don't, and they
just need your love

00:16:31.258 --> 00:16:32.357
then be there for them,

00:16:32.357 --> 00:16:35.489
but realize you must stay on your path

00:16:35.489 --> 00:16:37.406
regardless of jealousy.

